dressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO HIROYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIRASAKI YASUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJII, TAKAFUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITAYAMA, HIROKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIRASAKI, YASUO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Novel anthrapyridone compounds represented by formula (1) or salts thereof, which each has a hue and brightness suitable for ink-jet printing and gives a print excellent in fastness to light and water; a water-based magenta ink composition containing any of the compounds and salts; a method of ink-jet printing employing the same; and novel intermediates therefor. In said formula, R1 represents hydrogen, alkyl, etc.; R2 represents hydrogen, methyl, etc.; and X and Y each independently represents chlorine, hydroxy, etc.)</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne de nouveaux composés anthrapyridones représentés par la formule (1) ou leurs sels, chacun présentant une tonalité et une clarté se prêtant à l'impression par jet d'encre et dont la résistance à la lumière et à l'eau est excellente. L'invention concerne également une composition d'encre magenta à base d'eau renfermant tous les composés, leurs sels et un procédé d'impression par jet d'encre utilisant ces derniers et de nouveaux intermédiaires. Dans la formule, R1 représente un hydrogène, alkyle, etc.; R2 représente un hydrogène, méthyle, etc. et X et Y représentent, pris indépendamment, un chlore, hydroxy, etc.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>